1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,093
Afraid God is angry with you?

2
00:00:02,133 --> 00:00:03,960
Watch where Jesus stopped reading.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,740
In Nazareth, His home town,
He read God's promise

4
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,000
of someone sent with good news
for the poor,

5
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:11,230
and a time of God's welcome.

6
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:13,620
The prophet Isaiah's sentence goes on:

7
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:16,560
"and the day of vengeance of our God."

8
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:20,200
He left the day of vengeance unread,
and sat down.

9
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:23,750
"This day is this scripture fulfilled."

10
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:25,410
It was about Him.

11
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:28,120
They would want miracles, and say:

12
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,660
"Physician, heal thyself."

13
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:35,880
He reminded them God once sent help
to foreigners, not to their own.

14
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:39,320
Furious, they took Him to a cliff
to throw Him down.

15
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,480
He walked right through them.

16
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:44,400
Later, at the cross, the same dare:

17
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:47,160
"He saved others; let him save himself."

18
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:49,460
This time, He stayed.

19
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:52,170
He died, and rose again.

20
00:00:52,210 --> 00:00:54,450
He stopped reading at the welcome.

21
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:58,650
It is still open, for you, today.
